# Git branches

`main` is the normal version. Servers with beta off only update from `main`.
`beta` is the test channel. Servers with beta on update from `beta`.

- Push commits and open pull requests against `beta`.
- Do not push, merge, or fast-forward `main` unless the user explicitly asks to publish the normal version.
- Publishing the normal version means a fast-forward of `beta` onto `main`. No cherry-pick: non-beta servers must install the tree that was tested on beta.
- Do not put a semver tag (`v*`) on beta-only commits. The beta APK is the prerelease `android-beta`. The normal APK is `android-latest`, built from `main`.
